# ── Rust build artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/
**/target/
debug/
**/debug/

# Compiled libraries and objects
**/*.rlib
**/*.rmeta
**/*.d
**/*.o
**/*.a
**/*.pdb

# Shared / dynamic libraries
**/*.so
**/*.so.*
**/*.dylib
**/*.dll

# Z3 solver debug trace (written to cwd by bahyway-z3's dev-time-only tests)
.z3-trace

# Godot import/editor cache (generated per-machine by the engine, incl. PB-227's
# headless --import priming pass -- never hand-authored, never committed)
**/.godot/

# Executables and binaries
**/*.exe
**/*.out

# Incremental compilation state
**/incremental/
**/.fingerprint/
**/build/

# Rustfmt backup files
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo mutation testing output
**/mutants.out*/

# ── WASM / trunk build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
**/dist/
pkg/
**/pkg/
*.wasm

# ── IDE / editor state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/settings.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/tasks.json
.vscode/*.log
!.vscode/extensions.json

.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

.zed/

# DubSar IDE runtime state
*.dubsar-session
*.dubsar-cache

# ── OS-generated files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ── Logs and reports ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
*.report
*.log.gz

# ── Temporary / swap files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig

# ── Secrets and environment files ────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.cert

# ── Benchmark / profiling artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────
criterion/
flamegraph.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old

# ── Coverage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
lcov.info
coverage/
tarpaulin-report.html

# ── IsimudEngine generated reports (regenerated every run — not source) ──
# `docs/SHEDU/*` (not `docs/SHEDU/`) is deliberate: a directory-level
# pattern with a trailing slash prunes the whole directory from
# traversal, so a later per-file negation would be silently never
# evaluated (confirmed live via `git check-ignore -v` -- both a generated
# report AND an intended exception matched the same directory rule). The
# `*` form still ignores every file by default but keeps per-file
# negation usable if a future exception is ever needed again.
#
# 2026-08-15 doc taxonomy reorg: the 5 authored-content files that used
# to live under docs/SHEDU/ (and needed the negation exceptions this
# comment used to describe) moved to their real category homes
# (docs/16_runbooks/, docs/13_changelog/, docs/18_security/) -- none of
# which sit under any blanket ignore, so no exception is needed for them
# anymore. docs/SHEDU/ itself remains live and ignored: dozens of
# playbooks and anu-governor.toml's report_dir/chronicle_dir still write
# real run-output there.
docs/SHEDU/*
